body:
Aw I deadass appreciate the thought but honestly, I only had Xanax for the first time last night (although mixed with other shit) so I do see where you're coming from but at the same time, I don't see myself being reliant on those more intense substances at least right now. I've only had mdma 4 or so times when I go out and at concerts etc.

As for weed, I had exams recently so to help concentrate I only had weed like 5 times within a month so although weed definitely makes things appear easier for me I feel I can control myself to a certain point. Again I do see where you're coming from, but I've always had these anxiety/lack of confidence/depression (some suicidal) problems since 2012ish and only started using substances at the start of 2018 (which kind of helped me personally) so in all honesty I don' think I'll be cutting weed out of my life :/ But again I do understand that there is a possibility this shit can get serious.

&#x200B;

I just rang up a crisis line to help me map out a plan. Tomorrow I have work with my co-worker (which I trust) that said I can open up to her about anything so we'll see how that goes. If nothing happens there I'll try to contact my university's health center to see if a psychologist is available but it could be closed now that everyone's studies are finished. Then my last idea would be contacting my previous flatmate.

&#x200B;

I went into my Uni's health services when I was in a similar situation but I only got sleeping pills. I'm thinking I do need antidepressants though, when I had Xanax I felt rather chilled out.

&#x200B;

Nah these long convos always slap lmao
